  "negotiate": {
   "name": "negotiate",
   "node_type": "conversation",
   "on_enter": {"type": "llm", "prompt": "Say you are calling from the collections team about a late payment. State every late product from the facts, one sentence each, with its name, past-due amount and days late. Then ask: \"Can you make this payment today?\" (for several products, ask whether they can pay all of them today)."},
   "on_enter_first_entry_only": true,
   "task_message": "Facts (computed; use them exactly, never compute dates yourself):\n{{facts_text}}\n\nRules:\n- Ask for the full past-due amount first. Never ask how much they can pay; you propose every amount.\n- With several products, if they cannot pay all today, go through the products one by one in the order above, without asking about today again. Attempts count per product.\n- A date or amount the customer proposes is never a refusal. A promise date must be today or later, a business day, not after that product's deadline. A weekend or holiday not after the deadline: offer the next business day. After the deadline: say the latest date you can record is the deadline and offer it; refusing it is a flat refusal. Vague period: ask once for the exact day, then propose the deadline. 'Next <weekday>' is that weekday in the following calendar week; 'this <weekday>' is in the current week.\n- Amount from floor to full past due: accept. Full amount too much: offer the floor once and say the rest stays overdue. Below the floor: say it cannot be recorded and offer the floor once. Refusing the floor is a flat refusal.\n- A flat refusal or non-answer uses one persuasion attempt: make exactly the attempts listed for the product, never repeat a refused offer. When attempts are used up, call add_note with reason declined for that product and move on.\n- Illness, death in the family or job loss: one short sentence of sympathy, no persuasion, offer the support team. Accepts: transfer_to_agent queue support. Declines: add_note financial_difficulty for each product without a promise, then close.\n- 'I already paid': say payments can take one business day to appear; add_note already_paid for that product; continue with the others.\n- Not mine / never had it / closed or paid off before: do not argue; add_note contested for that product; continue with the others.\n- New payment plan or lower instalments: do not describe or discuss any plan, do not mention terms; first call add_note declined for every product without a recorded promise, then transfer_to_agent queue restructuring.\n- Human: ask once whether you can help; if they insist, transfer_to_agent queue general (no notes).\n- Customer says twice they do not want to talk: add_note declined for each open product, then close.\n- Before recording: read back every agreed product, amount and date together (say if a product is on its own deadline) and ask \"Do you confirm?\". Only after a clear yes call create_promise once per product with account_ref, amount_cents (whole cents from the facts or the agreed amount times 100) and date YYYY-MM-DD. If they change something, check it and read back again.\n- Say a promise is recorded only after create_promise returns ok. If it fails, try once more; if it fails again, say you could not record it and call add_note system_error for that product.\n- After recorded promises, say: \"You will receive a text message confirming each promise.\"\n- One promise per product; a recorded promise cannot be changed.\n- When every product is handled, thank the customer, say goodbye and call end_call.",
   "tools": [
    {"type": "function", "config": {"timeoutMs": 12000, "maxRetries": 0}, "function": {"name": "create_promise", "handler": "__function__:api_call", "description": "Record one payment promise. CALL it only after a clear yes to the read-back, once per product.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {
     "url": {"type": "string", "default": "https://bank-mock.invalid/f3-kestrel/v1/create_promise"},
     "method": {"type": "string", "default": "POST"},
     "headers": {"type": "object", "properties": {"Content-Type": {"type": "string", "default": "application/json"}}},
     "body": {"type": "object", "properties": {
      "customer_id": {"type": "string", "default": "{{customer_id}}"},
      "account_ref": {"type": "string", "description": "The product's account_ref from the facts.", "default": "{{account_ref}}"},
      "amount_cents": {"type": "integer", "description": "Amount in whole cents: 120.50 is 12050.", "default": "{{amount_cents}}"},
      "date": {"type": "string", "description": "YYYY-MM-DD, a business day not after the product's deadline.", "default": "{{date}}"}},
      "required": ["customer_id", "account_ref", "amount_cents", "date"]}}}},
     "pre_process_code": "import datetime\nimport json\nHOL = set(datetime.date.fromisoformat(x) for x in ['2026-10-12', '2026-11-11', '2026-11-26', '2026-11-27', '2026-12-25'])\n\ndef bd(d):\n    return d.weekday() < 5 and d not in HOL\n\ndef nbd(d):\n    d = d + datetime.timedelta(days=1)\n    while not bd(d):\n        d = d + datetime.timedelta(days=1)\n    return d\n\ntry:\n    vars['promise_block'] = ''\n    b = config.get('body')\n    if isinstance(b, dict):\n        facts = json.loads(vars.get('facts_json') or '[]')\n        ref = str(b.get('account_ref') or '')\n        vars['pending_ref'] = ref\n        f = next((x for x in facts if str(x.get('ref')) == ref), None)\n        done = json.loads(vars.get('promised_refs') or '[]')\n        v = float(str(b.get('amount_cents')).replace(',', '').strip())\n        cents = int(round(v)) if v == int(v) else int(round(v * 100))\n        msg = ''\n        if f is None:\n            msg = 'Unknown account_ref. Use the account_ref from the facts.'\n        else:\n            if cents < f['floor_cents'] and f['floor_cents'] <= cents * 100 <= f['past_cents']:\n                cents = cents * 100\n            b['amount_cents'] = cents\n            today = datetime.datetime.strptime(str(vars.get('now')).strip().replace(' ', 'T')[:16], '%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M').date()\n            dl = datetime.date.fromisoformat(f['deadline'])\n            day = datetime.date.fromisoformat(str(b.get('date')).strip()[:10])\n            b['date'] = day.isoformat()\n            if ref in done:\n                msg = 'This product already has a recorded promise; it cannot be changed. Do not record it again.'\n            elif day < today:\n                msg = 'That date is in the past. Offer a business day from today up to ' + dl.isoformat() + '.'\n            elif day > dl:\n                msg = 'After the deadline. Say the latest date you can record is ' + dl.isoformat() + ' and offer it.'\n            elif not bd(day):\n                nb = nbd(day)\n                msg = 'Not a business day. Offer ' + (nb.isoformat() if nb <= dl else dl.isoformat()) + ' instead.'\n            elif cents < f['floor_cents']:\n                msg = 'Below the floor: say it cannot be recorded and offer the floor (amount_cents ' + str(f['floor_cents']) + ') once.'\n            elif cents > f['past_cents']:\n                msg = 'More than the past-due amount. Use at most amount_cents ' + str(f['past_cents']) + '.'\n        if msg:\n            vars['promise_block'] = msg\n            b.pop('account_ref', None)\n            b['date'] = ''\nexcept Exception:\n    vars['promise_block'] = 'Amount or date could not be read. Ask again and use amount_cents in whole cents and date YYYY-MM-DD.'\n    try:\n        config.get('body').pop('account_ref', None)\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n",
     "post_process_code": "import json\ntry:\n    result.pop('header', None)\n    d = result.get('data')\n    block = vars.get('promise_block') or ''\n    if block:\n        if not isinstance(d, dict):\n            d = {}\n            result['data'] = d\n        d['ok'] = False\n        d['what_to_do_next'] = 'NOT recorded, nothing was sent. ' + block\n    elif isinstance(d, dict) and str(d.get('ok')).lower() == 'true':\n        vars['promise_count'] = str(int(vars.get('promise_count') or 0) + 1)\n        refs = json.loads(vars.get('promised_refs') or '[]')\n        refs.append(vars.get('pending_ref') or '')\n        vars['promised_refs'] = json.dumps(refs)\n        d['what_to_do_next'] = 'Recorded. Record the next agreed product if any; when all are recorded say: You will receive a text message confirming each promise.'\n    elif isinstance(d, dict):\n        d['what_to_do_next'] = 'Not recorded. Try once more with the same values; if it already failed twice, say you could not record it and call add_note with reason system_error.'\n    else:\n        result['what_to_do_next'] = 'Not recorded. Try once more with the same values; if it already failed twice, say you could not record it and call add_note with reason system_error.'\nexcept Exception:\n    pass\n"},
    {"type": "function", "config": {"timeoutMs": 12000, "maxRetries": 0}, "function": {"name": "add_note", "handler": "__function__:api_call", "description": "Record why a product ended without a promise. CALL it once for each such product.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {
     "url": {"type": "string", "default": "https://bank-mock.invalid/f3-kestrel/v1/add_note"},
     "method": {"type": "string", "default": "POST"},
     "headers": {"type": "object", "properties": {"Content-Type": {"type": "string", "default": "application/json"}}},
     "body": {"type": "object", "properties": {
      "customer_id": {"type": "string", "default": "{{customer_id}}"},
      "account_ref": {"type": "string", "description": "The product's account_ref.", "default": "{{account_ref}}"},
