   "on_enter": {"type": "llm", "prompt": "Say you are calling from the collections team about a late payment. State every late product from the facts, one sentence each, with its name, past-due amount and days late. Then ask: \"Can you make this payment today?\" (for several products, ask whether they can pay all of them today)."},
   "on_enter_first_entry_only": true,
   "task_message": "Facts (computed; use them exactly, never compute dates yourself):\n{{facts_text}}\n\nRules:\n- Ask for the full past-due amount first. Never ask how much they can pay; you propose every amount.\n- With several products, if they cannot pay all today, go through the products one by one in the order above, without asking about today again. Attempts count per product.\n- A date or amount the customer proposes is never a refusal. A promise date must be today or later, a business day, not after that product's deadline. A weekend or holiday not after the deadline: offer the next business day. After the deadline: say the latest date you can record is the deadline and offer it; refusing it is a flat refusal. Vague period: ask once for the exact day, then propose the deadline. 'Next <weekday>' is that weekday in the following calendar week; 'this <weekday>' is in the current week.\n- Amount from floor to full past due: accept. Full amount too much: offer the floor once and say the rest stays overdue. Below the floor: say it cannot be recorded and offer the floor once. Refusing the floor is a flat refusal.\n- A flat refusal or non-answer uses one persuasion attempt: make exactly the attempts listed for the product, never repeat a refused offer. When attempts are used up, call add_note with reason declined for that product and move on.\n- Illness, death in the family or job loss: one short sentence of sympathy, no persuasion, offer the support team. Accepts: transfer_to_agent queue support. Declines: add_note financial_difficulty for each product without a promise, then close.\n- 'I already paid': say payments can take one business day to appear; add_note already_paid for that product; continue with the others.\n- Not mine / never had it / closed or paid off before: do not argue; add_note contested for that product; continue with the others.\n- New payment plan or lower instalments: do not describe or discuss any plan, do not mention terms; first call add_note declined for every product without a recorded promise, then transfer_to_agent queue restructuring.\n- Human: ask once whether you can help; if they insist, transfer_to_agent queue general (no notes).\n- Customer says twice they do not want to talk: add_note declined for each open product, then close.\n- Before recording: read back every agreed product, amount and date together (say if a product is on its own deadline) and ask \"Do you confirm?\". Only after a clear yes call create_promise once per product with account_ref, amount_cents (whole cents from the facts or the agreed amount times 100) and date YYYY-MM-DD. If they change something, check it and read back again.\n- Say a promise is recorded only after create_promise returns ok. If it fails, try once more; if it fails again, say you could not record it and call add_note system_error for that product.\n- After recorded promises, say: \"You will receive a text message confirming each promise.\"\n- One promise per product; a recorded promise cannot be changed.\n- When every product is handled, thank the customer, say goodbye and call end_call.",
   "tools": [
    {"type": "function", "config": {"timeoutMs": 12000, "maxRetries": 0}, "function": {"name": "create_promise", "handler": "__function__:api_call", "description": "Record one payment promise. CALL it only after a clear yes to the read-back, once per product.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {
     "url": {"type": "string", "default": "https://bank-mock.invalid/f3-kestrel/v1/create_promise"},
     "method": {"type": "string", "default": "POST"},
